                "event": "Coastal Flood Watch",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Upton NY",
                "headline": "Coastal Flood Watch issued November 24 at 4:57PM EST until November 27 at 1:00PM EST by NWS Upton NY",
                "description": "* WHAT...1 to 2 ft of inundation above ground level possible in\nvulnerable areas near the waterfront and shoreline.\n\n* WHERE...New York (Manhattan), Richmond (Staten Island) and\nKings (Brooklyn) Counties.\n\n* WHEN...From Thursday morning through Friday afternoon high\ntides.\n\n* COASTAL FLOOD IMPACTS...Widespread minor to moderate flooding\nof vulnerable areas near the waterfront and shoreline,\nincluding roads, parking lots, parks, lawns, and homes and\nbusinesses with basements near the waterfront. Numerous road\nclosures are likely, and vehicles parked in vulnerable areas\nnear the waterfront will likely become flooded. Flooding will\nalso extend inland from the waterfront along tidal rivers and\nbays.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The highest water levels are likely with\nthe Thursday morning and evening high tides, potentially\nextending into the Friday morning high tides. The forecast has\nbeen leaned towards a higher end water level scenario to provide\na bit of safety margin. If the timing of strongest winds is\nquicker than currently forecast the peak water level forecast\ncould be increased by a few tenths for Thursday morning. if\nslower the Thursday morning forecast could be lowered slightly.",
                "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
                "response": "Prepare",
